# Cloud Logging MCP

Load [`docs/agents/mcp/cloud-logging.md`](docs/agents/mcp/cloud-logging.md).

Call `cloud-logging` only if `jarvis project show <name> --json` includes
`cloud-logging` in `project.mcp`. If the list is missing or empty, skip GCP
logs. Do not ask the user to connect Google Cloud.

Quota project is `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` / `logging.quota_project` on that
project yaml. Log location is `logging.resources` (`resourceNames`). Do not
use hub defaults for product GCP ids.

Prefer MCP `queryLogs` when the server is up. Else ADC `entries:list`.
Always set a time window. Prefer correlation-id structured filters.
Do not trust `aggregateLogs` as a total count.
